  "notes": "A terrace of three Cotswold cottages, 21 m by 5.5 m walls, 12 m to the ridge, under one stone-slate roof, split by two party walls, each with its own 1 m by 2.5 m painted door and hood. Faces local -Z; limestone quoins, sills and string course, stacks at both ends and on each party wall. Carves nothing.",
